              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lady Madonna"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Okay, I was a little wierded out by the thought of eating straight cabbage, but this dish is amazing! I also tried it with apple cider vinegar in place of the wine, and it's great either way."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "horsepro"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used 1 large Vidalia onion sliced into thin half circle strips, a medium head of cabbage cut into small strips. Then cooked it all in 2 Tbs of EVO with a Tbs of Ghee, ¼ cup Merlot, 1 Tbs low sodium Soy sauce. Then finished it all with a Tsp of corn starch to make the remaining liquid adhere to the cabbage and onion. Seasoned with fresh ground pepper and Himalayan fresh ground salt to taste. Cooked it all on a Wok on medium high. It turned out delicious.",
            "datePublished": "2019-03-27T22:44:53.470Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lutzflcat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We enjoy stir-fried/sauteed cabbage, but we thought the seasoning on this was weak. I didn’t have any Chinese cooking wine, so I sub’d dry sherry which worked out fine. I ended up doubling the soy sauce and sherry, and added some sliced bell pepper for a pop of color. Turned out pretty well, served with grilled, marinated flank steak..",
            "datePublished": "2023-11-13T11:25:53.000Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "UniqueDonut4844"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Absolutely LOVE this for simple prep, Asian flavor and healthy ingredients (cabbage, garlic). As someone else mentioned, great for a low carb diet. I use this cabbage to replace half - or all! - of the rice I’d normally eat alongside a more complex meat/vegetable dish. Also delicious on its own! (Of course the Shaoxing &amp; soy sauce add a little carb.) I used mirin in place of Shaoxing only because it was on hand. Turned out great. Shaoxing, though, will give you much richer flavor (maybe some of the commenters here didn’t have any or forgot to use a decent substitute). I’ll definitely be grabbing some Shaoxing next trip to the Asian grocery.",
            "datePublished": "2024-02-21T01:26:16.679Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
